@startuml Preciazo_Merchant_Management_States
title Preciazo - Fiscal Verification and Promotion Lifecycles (AV2)
skinparam shadowing false
hide empty description
state "Merchant fiscal verification" as Fiscal {
 state "PENDING" as FiscalPending
 state "VERIFIED" as FiscalVerified
 state "REJECTED" as FiscalRejected
 [*] --> FiscalPending : Request affiliation
 FiscalPending --> FiscalVerified : Provider returns ACTIVE
 FiscalPending --> FiscalRejected : Provider returns INACTIVE / NOT_FOUND
 FiscalPending --> FiscalPending : Provider failure
 note bottom of FiscalPending
  Retry requires the recorded owner.
  Fiscal verification does not prove ownership of the business.
  A read-only RUC preview never changes this state.
 end note
}
state "Promotion lifecycle" as Promo {
 state "SCHEDULED" as PromoScheduled
 state "ACTIVE" as PromoActive
 state "EXPIRED" as PromoExpired
 state "CANCELLED" as PromoCancelled
 state Creation <<choice>>
 [*] --> Creation : Create validated promotion
 Creation --> PromoScheduled : Start is in the future
 Creation --> PromoActive : startsAt <= now < endsAt
 PromoScheduled --> PromoScheduled : Edit before start
 PromoScheduled --> PromoActive : Activation job when due
 PromoScheduled --> PromoExpired : Job runs after the end
 PromoActive --> PromoExpired : End reached
 PromoScheduled --> PromoCancelled : Owner cancels
 PromoActive --> PromoCancelled : Owner cancels
 PromoExpired --> [*]
 PromoCancelled --> [*]
 note bottom of PromoScheduled
  Positive discounted price; end follows start; end must be in the future.
  Reject overlaps for the same store offer, with concurrency protection.
 end note
 note bottom of PromoActive
  Public queries always check the time window and current regular price.
  At or after the end, no promotional price is exposed even if a job is late.
  Normal catalog price is never overwritten by this lifecycle.
 end note
}
@enduml
